bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 8, "2026-11-27 residual (b) split out as seed_jit_erased_f64_option_some_binds_raw_bits_2026-11-27 (fix-implemented-verification-pending on work/bug-erased-f64-none-20261127: erased-parameter boundary hands f64?/Option<f64> Some over as a tagged float). Typed f64? Some readers losing the low mantissa bits filed as seed_jit_explicit_f64_option_some_typed_readers_lose_low_mantissa_bits_2026-11-27."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 6, "2026-11-27 re-review (a): the global enum table keeps no generic params, so a builtin-shaped Option<T> (src/compiler_rust/lib/std/src/core/option.spl: Some(T) | None) counted as a user Some-owning enum and switched the raw binding off. lowerer.rs global_def_is_builtin_option recognises that shape (Some payload naming a single-letter type param); stmt_lowering.rs exempts it, and a module.types Option when the global one is builtin. Red->green: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs global-table test 1000 -> 1012."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 5, "2026-11-27 review fix (Fable FIX-FIRST on d617c257cc3): a USER enum named Option (test/fixtures/user_option_enum_match) through an untyped param bound 42<<3 (336099 vs 42099) because the user-enum gate exempted the name Option. The gate now exempts only the generic builtin in module.types and counts every global_enum_defs enum declaring Some. Red->green: seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs user-Option test 336099 -> 42099. Seed e6c71f325bb533c2: raw parse/text/bool still bind (pm S12, pt, pv), fixture some_arm=42 none_arm=99 none_via_some=unmatched. Perf 3 alternated rounds 4e7 erased matches: org2 0.20/0.19/0.23s, fix 0.20/0.19/0.22s."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 7, "2026-11-27 residual (a) resolved on work/bug-any-some-arm-user-enum-20261127: the program-wide gate is replaced by a per-value runtime variant test, so a raw parse_int result binds 12 even when a Some-owning enum is declared (pg.spl JIT S12). Residual (b), boxed f64? payload bits, and the text-form representation remain open."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 4, "2026-11-27 residuals of the pattern-bind fix: (a) the gate is compile-time and program-wide: any program declaring a non-Option enum with a Some variant falls back to rt_enum_payload, so a raw parse_int result there still binds nil (pg.spl: JIT Snil, interp S12) -- follow-up is a runtime variant test, see seed_jit_any_match_bare_some_arm_takes_user_enum_unit_variant_2026-11-27. (b) pre-existing, unchanged: an explicit boxed f64? Some(1.5) through an untyped match binds raw bits 576179277326712832 on JIT (interp S1.5). Raw parse_float / text? / bool? now bind correctly (Rust test 4)."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 3, "2026-11-27 opus-bugbatch: FIXED erased-boundary pattern bind. match/if-val/match-expr Some(v) over an any subject holding a raw T? (parse_int result through an untyped param) bound v via rt_enum_payload => nil (JIT m=Snil, interp S12). hir/lower/stmt_lowering.rs build_pattern_binding_stmts now reads rt_unwrap_or_self for an ANY subject when no user enum declares Some (pattern name resolves to Option even for user enums). Red->green: compiler/tests/seed_jit_erased_option_some_pattern.rs (3 tests; 1000100695 -> 1012100695). Perf: 4e7 erased matches 0.22s org2 vs 0.20-0.23s fix. Probed: no raw-3 nil collision (\"3\".parse_int() = Some(3)). STILL OPEN (representation): through an untyped param the JIT prints parse results as 12/nil and explicit Some(12) as <enum@0x..> vs interpreter Option::Some(12)/Option::None; relay(x) returns raw. Handover spec test/01_unit/compiler/jit_erased_option_text_form_spec.spl (@tag:in-development, 4/4 red on JIT). Needs the dedicated primitive-T? boxing lane."
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 0, audit=triage-20261027-v4 assessed_sha=c0b3ad911f4cb00c0f3550b05baa8d06347d17d0 review=accepted inspection=source_reviewed validity=valid reproducibility=untested scope=UNRUN solution=unknown structural=unknown action=keep_open review_receipt=scoped_v3_aggregate evidence=doc/08_tracking/bug/triage_20261027/reviewed_categories_v4.sdn evidence_sha256=f47867ce23862fe32ca679bd72a0f53a2ea1e0727044f8c32f71209653d4da42 manifest_sha256=20c9585305077f9cdec78d82dee9f3add8fb1d98258b9209ad6169097072296c evidence_commit=b078b2807cf4379640f832a29672119f57e565ff scope_evidence=none scope_sha256=none record_sha256=ae9f68d9ad8c47685061aa200638f70d5d53154531fe67b54edb5fb8f808569a
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 1, "2026-11-10 status fixing->open: stale sweep claim, no lane active; reopened for P2 burn-down"
    parse_family_strips_option_jit_native_2026-08-02, 2, "2026-11-11 opus seed lane: status stays open. Re-verified on origin/release/1.0.0: rt_string_parse_int (runtime/src/value/collections.rs:6396) returns NIL/bare tagged int; primitive T? is by design a raw untagged payload-or-NIL-sentinel (runtime/src/value/sffi/io_print.rs rt_opt_i64_to_string doc; codegen/instr/mod.rs nil_tainted). Making parse_* yield Option::Some/None needs the seed-wide primitive-optional representation change (MIR lowering, HIR payload_slot_expr/lower_coalesce, cranelift+llvm call sites in codegen/instr/calls.rs, closures_structs.rs, llvm/functions*.rs) — not a single-site lane fix; partial change would desync the nil_tainted renderer. Seed is bootstrap-only; no spec or code landed. Direction decided by owner 2026-11-06 (seed .? = pure Simple parity): parse_* must return real Option Some/None on JIT/native matching interpreter; plan = seed-wide change across cranelift+llvm call sites, HIR/MIR lowering, nil print path, in a dedicated lane."

